From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:02:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/35] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt6878-titan2: RAW/YUV engines,
 -raw, -jpeg and -vcp test boards

- mt6878.dtsi: RAW-A/YUV-A and RAW-B/YUV-B engine nodes, disabled.
- -raw: -all plus larbs 16/17 and 33/34, the engines with RAW-B as the
  second engine of RAW-A, and RAW-A as the second destination of the main
  camera's CSI port. Needs the request dumps camraw-start.bin and
  camraw-frame.bin. A one-shot test board.
- -jpeg: -all plus the JPEG encoder behind the M4U (variant B).
- -vcp, -vcp-iommu: -all plus the VCP node, with vcp-support so that the
  boot loader loads the VCP firmware; -vcp-iommu puts the VCP behind the
  M4U.
- -all-iommu is now the same as -all (the display is behind the M4U on
  -all), kept for boot scripts.
- -cameras.dtsi: the MT6319 comment says "downstream kernel".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
